#!/bin/sh
# Prints the section of one version from CHANGELOG.md, for the release notes:
#   sh deploy/release-notes 1.0.0
# Fails when CHANGELOG.md has no "## [VERSION]" heading or the section is empty.
set -eu
version=${1:?usage: sh deploy/release-notes VERSION}
changelog=$(CDPATH= cd -- "$(dirname -- "$0")/.." && pwd)/CHANGELOG.md
notes=$(awk -v v="$version" '
  index($0, "## [" v "]") == 1 { on = 1; next }
  on && /^## \[/ { exit }
  on && /^\[[^]]*\]: / { exit }
  on { print }
' "$changelog" | sed -e '/./,$!d')
if [ -z "$notes" ]; then
  echo "rift: CHANGELOG.md has no notes under '## [$version]'" >&2
  exit 1
fi
printf '%s\n' "$notes"
